From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:21:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: core: handle absent codec children during
 recovery

The encoder and decoder are separate modules, and either of them may not
be bound when the firmware reports a system error. The recovery handler
waits for both to go idle and passes core->dev_dec and core->dev_enc to
pm_runtime_active() unconditionally, so it dereferences a NULL device
when only one of them is bound.

Treat an absent child as idle.

Fixes: 43e221e485e5 ("media: venus: Rework recovery mechanism")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index 3e69fc7ea3..ae3d446cc9 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -104,7 +104,8 @@ static void venus_sys_error_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 	core->state = CORE_UNINIT;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < max_attempts; i++) {
-		if (!pm_runtime_active(core->dev_dec) && !pm_runtime_active(core->dev_enc))
+		if ((!core->dev_dec || !pm_runtime_active(core->dev_dec)) &&
+		    (!core->dev_enc || !pm_runtime_active(core->dev_enc)))
 			break;
 		msleep(10);
 	}
